   "isFreePreview": true,
   "description": "Khung môn học theo syllabus FLM chính thức.",
   "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">PEB301 · Section 0 · Lesson 0.6</span>\n<h2>Student tasks & constructive questions</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">The rules you are held to (attendance, preparation, exam eligibility) — verbatim.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM · Syllabus ID 13935 · Decision 1402/QĐ-ĐHFPT dated 12/12/2025 · collected 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">PEB301 · Mục 0 · Bài 0.6</span>\n<h2>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên & câu hỏi kiến tạo</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Những quy định bạn phải tuân theo (chuyên cần, chuẩn bị bài, điều kiện dự thi) — nguyên văn.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: FLM · Syllabus ID 13935 · QĐ 1402/QĐ-ĐHFPT ngày 12/12/2025 · thu ngày 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student tasks (verbatim)</h3>\n<p>- Attend at least 80% of lab sessions to be eligible for final assessment.<br><br>- Prepare before each lab by reviewing related theories and instructions provided by the instructor.<br><br>- Complete all assigned lab tasks, exercises, and reports on time, both individually and in groups.<br><br>- Use laptops, development boards, and lab equipment strictly for learning and project purposes.<br><br>- Maintain a lab notebook documenting circuit assembly, wiring diagrams, code, measurements, and observations.<br><br>- Actively participate in assembling, connecting, and programming microcontroller-based systems, testing functionality of peripherals (GPIO, ADC, timers, SPI, I2C, UART).<br><br>- Collaborate in team-based lab projects, demonstrating the integration of hardware and software into a complete embedded system.<br><br>- Apply theories from embedded system courses into practice, and seek feedback from instructors to improve performance and understanding.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên (nguyên văn)</h3>\n<p>- Attend at least 80% of lab sessions to be eligible for final assessment.<br><br>- Prepare before each lab by reviewing related theories and instructions provided by the instructor.<br><br>- Complete all assigned lab tasks, exercises, and reports on time, both individually and in groups.<br><br>- Use laptops, development boards, and lab equipment strictly for learning and project purposes.<br><br>- Maintain a lab notebook documenting circuit assembly, wiring diagrams, code, measurements, and observations.<br><br>- Actively participate in assembling, connecting, and programming microcontroller-based systems, testing functionality of peripherals (GPIO, ADC, timers, SPI, I2C, UART).<br><br>- Collaborate in team-based lab projects, demonstrating the integration of hardware and software into a complete embedded system.<br><br>- Apply theories from embedded system courses into practice, and seek feedback from instructors to improve performance and understanding.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Everything in the tables above is copied <strong>verbatim</strong> from the university's FLM page (in English, as published) so you can check it against the copy your lecturer gives you: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13935\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13935</a> (needs your FPT login). If FLM publishes a newer syllabus, FLM wins.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Mọi thứ trong các bảng trên được chép <strong>nguyên văn</strong> từ trang FLM của trường (bằng tiếng Anh, đúng như trường công bố) để bạn đối chiếu với bản giảng viên phát: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13935\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13935</a> (cần đăng nhập tài khoản FPT). Nếu FLM công bố bản syllabus mới hơn thì theo FLM.</div></div>"
